{
  "case_id": "2021-20-1800",
  "document_hash": "ecf79e111aaf5fa85d7a9214b5f8c925fe9a872e3e9434661c76262b42f8b6b0",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1800",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ecf79e111aaf5fa85d7a9214b5f8c925fe9a872e3e9434661c76262b42f8b6b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ecf79e111aaf-0000-0009",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for\noral argument before the Supreme Court of the\nUnited States at 10:00 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "City of Boston",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1800",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ecf79e111aaf5fa85d7a9214b5f8c925fe9a872e3e9434661c76262b42f8b6b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ecf79e111aaf-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The City's flag-raising forum is not\ngovernment speech under Walker and Summum. The City, by an unbroken history and practice and\npolicy, expressly declared that the flagpoles are one of its public forums open to all\napplicants. In doing so, the City long ago\ncrossed the line from government speech to private speech."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1800",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ecf79e111aaf5fa85d7a9214b5f8c925fe9a872e3e9434661c76262b42f8b6b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ecf79e111aaf-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Mr. Staver, you begin\nyour brief by arguing that this is a limited public forum and -- or a designated public\nforum. And do we have to agree with that in\norder for you to win?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1800",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ecf79e111aaf5fa85d7a9214b5f8c925fe9a872e3e9434661c76262b42f8b6b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ecf79e111aaf-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Can the City allow\npatriotic flags or messages of support and not those that are anti-American? For example, to\npick up on Justice Kagan's question, someone\nwants to fly the al Qaeda flag at City Hall in\nBoston."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1800",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ecf79e111aaf5fa85d7a9214b5f8c925fe9a872e3e9434661c76262b42f8b6b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ecf79e111aaf-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: But it just cried out with an empty record sort of for --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1800",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ecf79e111aaf5fa85d7a9214b5f8c925fe9a872e3e9434661c76262b42f8b6b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ecf79e111aaf-0001-0000",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Like any private property owner, the government is entitled to use its own property for whatever lawful purpose it likes, including for expressive purposes, and when the government expresses its own viewpoint, it is never compelled to express competing or alternative viewpoints."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1800",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ecf79e111aaf5fa85d7a9214b5f8c925fe9a872e3e9434661c76262b42f8b6b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ecf79e111aaf-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: So, Mr. Joshi, suppose you're right as to all of those things, that there was essentially no control from the city government here and -- and that pushes strongly in the direction of, well, it's not government speech if government doesn't control it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1800",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "ecf79e111aaf5fa85d7a9214b5f8c925fe9a872e3e9434661c76262b42f8b6b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ecf79e111aaf-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So the nature of the forum is important. So do you agree with your -- with Petitioner that forum is irrelevant in this case? And if you do, why is it irrelevant in this case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1800",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "ecf79e111aaf5fa85d7a9214b5f8c925fe9a872e3e9434661c76262b42f8b6b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ecf79e111aaf-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The sole issue here is whether the City's decision to lower Boston's flag from the City Hall flagpole and raise another in its place is the City's own speech. If so, then, as Summum held, the City is free to select the views it wants to express."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1800",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "ecf79e111aaf5fa85d7a9214b5f8c925fe9a872e3e9434661c76262b42f8b6b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ecf79e111aaf-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But do you think the fact that it is a flagpole in front of City Hall is dispositive?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Becket Fund",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1800",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "ecf79e111aaf5fa85d7a9214b5f8c925fe9a872e3e9434661c76262b42f8b6b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ecf79e111aaf-0002-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think the Becket Fund amicus brief is pretty helpful on that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1800",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ecf79e111aaf5fa85d7a9214b5f8c925fe9a872e3e9434661c76262b42f8b6b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ecf79e111aaf-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: But you're saying, Mr. Hallward-Driemeier, that we should recognize as government speech a program that basically now says and --and -- and,"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1800",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ecf79e111aaf5fa85d7a9214b5f8c925fe9a872e3e9434661c76262b42f8b6b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ecf79e111aaf-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: So -- so, counsel, if I understand your response, and I don't mean to interrupt, but -- but your -- your argument to Justice Kagan seems to hinge on a factual premise. Is this flagpole, in fact, open to all comers more or less? Is it a public forum?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "City of Boston",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1800",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ecf79e111aaf5fa85d7a9214b5f8c925fe9a872e3e9434661c76262b42f8b6b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ecf79e111aaf-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HALLWARD-DRIEMEIER: If the flagpoles had become a public forum, that was not our intent, but if by miscommunication the flagpoles were deemed a public forum, the City acknowledges it cannot exclude religious speech, it cannot exclude offensive speech or discriminatory speech from the flagpole because it -- it has to be viewpoint neutral."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1800",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ecf79e111aaf5fa85d7a9214b5f8c925fe9a872e3e9434661c76262b42f8b6b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ecf79e111aaf-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: But you -- you've said that if you lose this case, you would restructure your program so that you would be able to exercise the kind of control to exclude religious flags like, you know, the one that Camp Constitution wanted to fly."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mathew Staver",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1800",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ecf79e111aaf5fa85d7a9214b5f8c925fe9a872e3e9434661c76262b42f8b6b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ecf79e111aaf-0004-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STAVER: The record does reflect\nthat at the time, 2017, the website was in\neffect. In fact, that's what Hal Shurtleff\nused, and the policies specifically written by\nthe City for 2005 to 2017 include the statement\nthat these are public forums open to all\napplicants. And that's the application that\nstill is there, and it's still being used, and\nit's the same exact guidelines in 2017 as it is\nnow.\nIn 2019 -- and page 30 footnote of our\nbrief -- we indicate that during an\ninterrogatory, the City confirmed that all the\nHeritage Reporting Corporation"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mathew Staver",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1800",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ecf79e111aaf5fa85d7a9214b5f8c925fe9a872e3e9434661c76262b42f8b6b0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ecf79e111aaf-0004-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 91,
        "start": 91
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STAVER: The error of the First\nCircuit, Mr. Chief Justice, was to begin with\nthe notion that you can never have a flagpole\nforum. And then they crammed everything else\ninto government speech, foregoing the\ntraditional analysis of public forum doctrine."
    },
    {
